🚽 Test case: #193 -- returning a by-value struct member whose type does
🚽 not match the declared return type (`bussin b.s;` where `s` is a `gang
🚽 Small` but the function returns `gang Point`) is rejected at the return
🚽 statement -- the member-access counterpart of struct_return_type_
🚽 mismatch_fail (PR #253 review, finding 3).
gang Small {
    rizz x;
};
gang Point {
    rizz a;
    rizz b;
};
gang Box {
    gang Small s;
};

gang Point wrong_return(gang Box b) {
    bussin b.s;
}

skibidi main {
    gang Box bx;
    gang Point p = wrong_return(bx);
    bussin 0;
}
